{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552750-v5-predator-types-for-thin-bloods","id":1552750,"title":"V5 - Predator Types for Thin-Bloods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-30T11:09:04-07:00","id":1552750,"title":"V5 - Predator Types for Thin-Bloods","content":"Do you allow Thin-Bloods to have a Predator Type? Why or why not? If yes, does it affect the way they're played? If not, how do you explain them not having a favored way to feed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T11:32:12-07:00","id":1552751,"title":"","content":"I do not play V5 and have not read its corebook, but my understanding is that Predator Types are simply a way to provide some additional dots of Disciplines and Backgrounds or other character sheet mechanics tied to some flavor text. It's very similar to the Backgrounds in D&amp;D5e which, again, is just flavor text combined with some additional proficiencies and equipment. It's a quick and easy way to customize your character, and fairly easy for the ST to create/approve new Predator Types or D&amp;D Backgrounds based on new themes.<br /> <br /> If Thin Bloods in V5 still used Disciplines, there should be no problem allowing them. However, V5 Thin Bloods don't use Disciplines. Instead they utilize Thin Blood Alchemy and Blood Resonance. So if you want to use something like Predator Types, an ST needs to make necessary adjustments so that it makes sense with the new mechanics. So instead of Disciplines, maybe it provides additional Formulae for Blood Alchemy. Or maybe they lean more on additional Backgrounds or Abilities. Whatever makes sense for game balance purposes and can be tied together in a common theme. <br /> <br /> How many mechanic bonuses they should add really depends on how much the ST wants to give. Some STs may see Thin Bloods as needing to start out much weaker, and they may not want to give anything at all. Others may want Thin Blood characters to be just as &quot;useful&quot; as other PCs so may give them big bonuses.<br /> <br /> Preadtor Types are just a way to customize characters with additional character sheet powers, and to help jumpstart players to think more about the roleplaying aspects of their characters. If Predator Types are not given, it is not that those characters don't have a favored way to feed. They just lack the build points other characters get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T22:42:37-07:00","id":1552760,"title":"","content":"It's basically that.<br /> <br /> While the idea of giving them Predator Types isn't necessarily bad, mechanically they're not compatible with the rules for Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> Not a terribly hard thing to adapt, but still a lot of extra work as you have to decide if, and with what you'll replace the Discipline dots, and the Merits and Flaws given may not be the best choices for a Thin Blood following that types (as they're built upon the assumption of a regular Vampire behind them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T01:22:20-07:00","id":1552764,"title":"","content":"Didn't Justin anchilli say something about your predator type being more important than clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T09:55:23-07:00","id":1553029,"title":"","content":"I would, but I also think that predator types should be decoupled from disciplines.I like predator types in principle, because that's how vampires subsist as vampires, but I'd not rather push players who want 3 dots of Auspex to choose between Sandman and Consensualist. <br /> <br /> And ultimately I think that predator types should be a guide. So players could make their own or tweak an existing one, provided it balances with the others. Maybe older vampires could have stronger predator types, but that's a bit complicated compared to just letting them have more xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T12:50:20-07:00","id":1553033,"title":"","content":"Predator Types could have a role similar to the old Nature, that helped recover Willpower, or to Requiem's Conditions that help you get XP. Basically a small benefit that doesn't really change your power level, but rewards your acting out the Predator Type. That would make it more dynamic and relevant, give you more freedom at building your character and would be easy to apply to any character you need to cover.<br /> <br /> But as is, it simply can't be applied as is to <b>Thin Bloods</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T11:11:06-07:00","id":1553041,"title":"","content":"The paragraph in the character creation sections says fresh blood suckers. So I would think that a thinblood who's been around for a little bit would have their preferred method of hunting. <br /> I give them every from a PT except disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 